WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.534
-Welcome to
"The Tonight Show," you guys!

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.701
I'm so excited about this.

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.033
Taylor Swift
is my guest tonight.

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:07.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.634
♪♪

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:13.234
Yeah.
It's incredible.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:16.000
While you were just applauding,
Taylor wrote three more albums.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.067
She is unbelievable.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.367
Loving "Midnights."

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:21.434
Let's get to some news.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:22.934
Well, guys, President Biden says

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:25.934
that he plans to run
for re-election in 2024.

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:27.334
Meanwhile,
at a rally this weekend,

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.601
President Trump
also hinted at running.

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:32.300
It's big news, but all I can
think about is Taylor Swift

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.133
being on the show tonight, so...

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:40.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.033
So you know what that means.

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:44.334
It's time for
"The News: Taylor's Version."

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:46.033
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.534
♪♪

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:51.701
-So, Biden and Trump are both
running for re-election,

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:53.601
and they've got major
"bad blood,"

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:56.434
which everyone knows
"all too well."

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:59.167
Of course, Trump has quite
the "reputation."

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:01.968
Every other day, he's like,
"I did something bad,"

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:03.434
and Biden has to be like,

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.067
"This is why we can't have
nice things,"

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:08.300
which is why this could be
the most dramatic election

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.434
ever -- more --
Importantly --

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:14.434
"Evermore" importantly,
they both need running mates.

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:17.200
Biden is looking at Kamala like,
"You belong with me,"

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.400
while Trump is looking
at Mike Pence like,

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.734
"We are never ever
getting back together."

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:26.133
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.734
Like, ever.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.801
Pence is actually considering
a run of his own,

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.868
but everyone is like,
"I forgot that you existed."

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.667
"Long story short,"
everyone is tired of politics.

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:37.834
But, hey,
"you need to calm down,"

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:40.100
"shake it off,"
and get "ready for it,"

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.501
because "'tis the damn season."
So --

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:44.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:47.901
Go get your voting "card again,"

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.300
head to the polls --

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.000
Yeah, that was a stretch,
that one.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.467
Head to the polls and fill in
every "blank space."

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.801
It doesn't matter
if you're blue or "red"

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.501
or even a "lavender haze."

00:01:57.501 --> 00:02:00.367
You've got to let your voice
be heard,

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:03.834
both in 2024 and during
the midterms in "'22."

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:06.200
This has been
"The News: Taylor's Version."

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:10.634
♪♪

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:12.367
"Card again."
-Yeah.

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:14.367
-No, that was awful.
That was a stretch there.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.133
Yeah, that's right.
Biden intends to run again.

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:19.734
And in a recent interview
on MSNBC, he was asked

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.467
about his concerns over his age.

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:23.367
Check out the President's
response right here.

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:26.300
--I think it's a legitimate
thing to be concerned

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.567
about anyone's age,
including mine.

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:30.534
That's not how I feel.

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:33.434
I can't even say
the age I'm gonna be.

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:36.133
I can't even
get it out of my mouth.

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:39.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:41.300
-I've heard of people
dancing around their age,

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:42.400
but I've never seen someone

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.400
actually dance
around their age, like...

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:48.934
Eventually, a middle school nun
stepped in, like,

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.100
"Leave room for the Holy Ghost.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.167
Leave -- Leave room
for the Holy Ghost."

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.767
Secret Service
didn't know what to do.

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:55.868
They were like, "Should we step
in or give them alone time?

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:58.067
What's the call here?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.067 --> 00:02:59.934
Some more political news --
over the weekend,

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:02.534
former president Trump
held a rally in Texas,

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:03.901
and I noticed that he had
some trouble

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:05.767
with the word "smuggler."
Watch this.

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:09.501
-They deliberately surrendered
our border to vicious coyotes

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:12.100
and drug smaller --
I mean, these drug smug--

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.701
the smuggler.
A smuggler!

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:17.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:19.534
-"These drug snugglers --
drug smuckers --

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:22.734
drug snickerdoodles, they --"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:24.534
He sounds like he took
whatever illegal drug

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:27.701
is being "smullered"
across the border.

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:29.868
Sounds like a guy trying
to do his first Wordle.

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:31.667
It's like, "Small?
Smug?

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:33.901
Is smulg a word?

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.567
I'm gonna try 'smulg' anyway.
Why not?

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:37.501
Let's see.
Oh, I'm very smart."

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.334
Speaking of Trump,
the January 6th Committee

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:42.167
announced that they have
subpoenaed the former president.

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:43.834
Yep, Trump's already
bragging like,

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.033
"I've got the biggest subpoena.

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:47.133
I've been saying it for years.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:49.234
Nobody's subpoena
is bigger than mine."

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:52.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:53.601
Yep, the committee was like,

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:55.734
"Here's a federal document
that you can keep."

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:57.567
Yeah.
[ Audience groans ]

00:03:57.567 --> 00:04:00.701
Some big news from overseas --
today, Britain announced that

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:03.701
Rishi Sunak is going to be
their new prime minister

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:07.167
after Liz Truss lasted only
six weeks in office.

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:09.300
Yeah, when he showed up to his
new office, people were like,

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.934
"You can unpack your things,
but I wouldn't hang up

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:13.100
anything on the walls."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.334
Yeah, on Thursday,
after 45 days in office,

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:17.267
Liz Truss
announced her resignation

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:19.300
as prime minister of Britain.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.467
Let's take a look back

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.534
on all the greatest moments
of Liz Truss.

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:25.968
♪♪

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:27.033
-Good afternoon.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:27.934
♪♪

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:35.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:38.200
-Well, some sports news --
the World Series matchup

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.701
is set with the Houston Astros

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:41.601
taking on
the Philadelphia Phillies.

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:43.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
And, of course --

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:45.601
♪♪

00:04:45.601 --> 00:04:48.667
Of course, the fans from
Philadelphia are super pumped.

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:49.968
Check out this video.

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:52.667
-Let's go, Philly!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:54.234
-I'm feeling great!

00:04:54.234 --> 00:04:56.033
Four more!

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:57.300
-Come on, Phillies!

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.367
Four more!
World Series, baby!

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.968
-We got married on Friday,
and the Phillies won!

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:05.400
-This is the best part
of the weekend, by far!

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:11.734
-Oh!
"By far"?

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.567
-"By far."
-Oh, my God.

00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:15.767
-A lot of people have videos
of the moment they got married,

00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:17.267
but very few have a video
of the moment

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:18.934
their marriage fell apart.
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:20.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:23.100
Finally, scientists in Japan
have gotten closer to finding

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:25.067
a cure for baldness
after they were able

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:27.567
to grow hair follicles in a lab.

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:29.567
Well, they actually grew them
just outside the lab,

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:31.200
then they combed them over
into the lab.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.467
[ Laughter ]
We have a great show.

